2026-10-09T03:57:11.0419439Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0426992Z [1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer[0m
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0500638Z [32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0507963Z [0m
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0508335Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0508664Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0509524Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0509749Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0510211Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0510492Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0510665Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0510946Z    if you are ready to continue.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0511077Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0511426Z 3. Create the system users [34m(uids [30001..30008])[0m and groups [34m(gid 30000)[0m
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0511752Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0511999Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0512186Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0512276Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0512424Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0512702Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0512862Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0513080Z    can use Nix.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0513158Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0513224Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0513305Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0513595Z [32m[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0514026Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0519474Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0519748Z I will:
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0519870Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0520020Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0520392Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0520769Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0521086Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0521298Z  - install Nix in /nix
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0521602Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0521838Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0522059Z    /root
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0532251Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0532768Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0541510Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0541955Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0542132Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0543301Z [32m[4;32mReady to continue?
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0543742Z [0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0556890Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0557390Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0564620Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0564940Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0565198Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0565367Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0565517Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0565691Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0565899Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0566255Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0566422Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0566515Z If you would like to
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0566746Z see the output, try like this:
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0566888Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0567055Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0567339Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0567457Z 
2026-10-09T03:57:11.0567576Z 
